{"schema_version": 1, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T14:53:11.515789", "run_id": "ab-real_llm-overflow_scorer-s2-B-20261020145217", "task_id": "overflow_scorer", "seed": 2, "iteration": 1, "mode": "meta_controller_on", "judge": {"judge_type": "llm", "model_name": "openai/gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "provider": "openai", "model": "gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07", "call_args": {}, "max_parse_retries": 1}, "validator": {"name": "overflow_scorer_truth", "higher_is_better": true, "top_k": 5, "ranking": "population order (system ranking)", "draws": {"validation": 48, "test": 256, "calibration": 64}, "synthetic": true}, "acceptance_rule": {"split": "validation", "seeds": [3000, 3001], "min_improvement": 0.02, "rule": "accept iff all trials ran, no constraint violation, budget not exceeded, and mean(candidate) - mean(baseline) > 0 and >= min_improvement"}, "accepted_state_version_before": 0, "decision": {"failure_location": "implementation", "root_cause_hypothesis": "The quality_score scorer or its reporting pipeline is producing unscaled/unbounded outputs (observed mean 4.842e8 \u00b1 5.34e6, best ~4.851e8) instead of the documented [0,1] range \u2014 likely an implementation/reporting bug.", "intervention_target": "implementation", "rationale": "Quality_score values (mean ~4.842e8) are far outside the documented [0,1] range and will dominate the optimization. Sanitizing quality_score outputs to the valid range [0,1] will immediately prevent these outliers from driving selection, restoring balance so parameter_mean (mean 0.6913) and parameter_spread (mean 0.2889 vs target 0.15) can influence search while the root bug is investigated.", "proposed_change": {"objective_name": "quality_score", "action": "sanitize_outputs", "valid_range": [0.0, 1.0]}, "expected_benefit_hypothesis": "Prevents extreme quality_score values from dominating optimization decisions. This should restore meaningful multi-objective tradeoffs so parameter_mean and parameter_spread objectives affect selection, allow detection of the scorer bug, and produce more interpretable objective logs.", "validation_plan_suggested_by_judge": "Run the next optimization iteration(s) and confirm that quality_score evaluations are either within [0,1] or flagged as failed (no O(1e8) values). Check that optimization decisions are no longer dominated by a single objective (e.g., parameter_mean remains ~0.69 but parameter_spread does not continue moving further from 0.15). The validator should observe improved balance compared to the current state where extreme quality_score values dominate.", "self_reported_confidence_uncalibrated": 0.8}, "notes": [], "judge_raw_output": "Rationale (brief):\nThe analyzer shows quality_score values are O(1e8) (mean 4.842e8 \u00b1 5.34e6; best ~4.851e8), which contradicts the documented [0,1] range and will dominate optimization (risking ignoring parameter_mean and parameter_spread). The most direct, low-risk mitigation is to sanitize quality_score outputs so out-of-range values are treated as failed evaluations; this prevents the broken large values from dominating the aggregator and lets the optimizer meaningfully use the other objectives while the scorer bug is investigated.\n\n<decision>\n{\n  \"failure_location\": \"implementation\",\n  \"root_cause_hypothesis\": \"The quality_score scorer or its reporting pipeline is producing unscaled/unbounded outputs (observed mean 4.842e8 \u00b1 5.34e6, best ~4.851e8) instead of the documented [0,1] range \u2014 likely an implementation/reporting bug.\",\n  \"intervention_target\": \"implementation\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Quality_score values (mean ~4.842e8) are far outside the documented [0,1] range and will dominate the optimization. Sanitizing quality_score outputs to the valid range [0,1] will immediately prevent these outliers from driving selection, restoring balance so parameter_mean (mean 0.6913) and parameter_spread (mean 0.2889 vs target 0.15) can influence search while the root bug is investigated.\",\n  \"proposed_change\": {\n    \"objective_name\": \"quality_score\",\n    \"action\": \"sanitize_outputs\",\n    \"valid_range\": [\n      0.0,\n      1.0\n    ]\n  },\n  \"expected_benefit\": \"Prevents extreme quality_score values from dominating optimization decisions. This should restore meaningful multi-objective tradeoffs so parameter_mean and parameter_spread objectives affect selection, allow detection of the scorer bug, and produce more interpretable objective logs.\",\n  \"validation_plan\": \"Run the next optimization iteration(s) and confirm that quality_score evaluations are either within [0,1] or flagged as failed (no O(1e8) values). Check that optimization decisions are no longer dominated by a single objective (e.g., parameter_mean remains ~0.69 but parameter_spread does not continue moving further from 0.15). The validator should observe improved balance compared to the current state where extreme quality_score values dominate.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.8\n}\n</decision>", "change_id": "1afed3924a02b855", "candidate_state": {"version": 0, "planner_guidance": null, "objective_ops": [], "implementation_patches": {"quality_score": {"action": "sanitize_outputs", "valid_range": [0.0, 1.0]}}, "workflow_params": {}}, "validation": {"seeds": [3000, 3001], "use_planner": false, "candidate_objectives": ["quality_score", "parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline_objectives": ["quality_score", "parameter_mean", "parameter_spread"], "baseline": [2.629905878029909e-06, 1.2808647926225434e-05], "candidate": [0.00011316978743669884, 0.05200441293760015], "baseline_mean": 7.719276902127672e-06, "candidate_mean": 0.026058791362518423, "delta": 0.026051072085616297, "min_improvement": 0.02, "candidate_constraint_violation": false, "details": {"baseline": [{"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_quality": 2.0790025852507166e-05, "population_mean": 5.9804140048532e-06, "best": 4.1665238431016706e-05, "n_invalid": 0}, {"split": "validation", "top_k": 5, "top_k_by_true_qua